\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {PriVoke}\xspace  's client, server and opt-in legacy training paths. Local inspection returns an action: ALLOW and WARN send the original body; BLOCK cancels the request. Randomized coarse event fields pass through a separate budgeted reporting channel. Standard V3 uses pinned read-only packages. In the legacy route, the updater requests a cycle; the fuzzer generates labelled examples, the server runtime computes bounded updates on its cached model, and the fuzzer forwards only candidates passing its held-out guards. The updater applies an update only to its exact parent; this dashed path does not update standard V3.}}{4}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{\privoke 's client, server and opt-in legacy training paths. Local inspection returns an action: ALLOW and WARN send the original body; BLOCK cancels the request. Randomized coarse event fields pass through a separate budgeted reporting channel. Standard V3 uses pinned read-only packages. In the legacy route, the updater requests a cycle; the fuzzer generates labelled examples, the server runtime computes bounded updates on its cached model, and the fuzzer forwards only candidates passing its held-out guards. The updater applies an update only to its exact parent; this dashed path does not update standard V3}{figure.caption.7}{}}
